year={1991},
annote={Presents an engineering approach to the design of
distributed real-time systems, which guarantee hard
deadlines and can tolerate a specified set of faults.
The methodology covers the stepwise refinement of the
given requirements, expressed in the form of real-time
transactions, to task and protocol executions. It also
includes a timing analysis and dependability
evaluation of the still incomplete design. The
testability of the evolving system is considered to be
