note={Commun. ACM (USA)},
month={Feb.},
year={1980},
annote={The use of monitors for describing concurrency has been
much discussed in the literature. When monitors are
used in real systems of any size, however, a number of
problems arise which have not been adequately dealt
with: the semantics of nested monitor calls; the
various ways of defining the meaning of WAIT, priority
scheduling; handling of timeouts, aborts and other
